# Patterns match the full path RELATIVE TO THE BUILD CONTEXT ROOT, and `*` does not
# cross `/`. So a bare name matches only at the root — unlike `.gitignore`, where a
# slash-free pattern matches at every depth. (Explicit depth patterns are valid, e.g.
# `projects/api/uploads`; what a bare name cannot do is reach depth implicitly.)
# The bare names below are therefore correct for the STANDALONE build this file
# serves: context = this repo root, single package, no nested copies.
#
# In an lt-monorepo this file is INERT. `lt fullstack init` places this project at
# `projects/api/`, and both images build with the monorepo root as context — BuildKit
# looks for `<dockerfile-path>.dockerignore` first and then `<context>/.dockerignore`,
# neither of which is this file. Put rules in the monorepo's `/.dockerignore` (see
# lt-monorepo), in `**/` form. Note the trap: renaming this file to
# `Dockerfile.dockerignore` WOULD revive it, but its bare patterns would then anchor
# at the MONOREPO root — `tests` would target `<monorepo>/tests`, not this project's.
# Inert is the safer of the two failure modes; do not "fix" it that way.

# Dependencies
node_modules
.pnpm-store

# Build output
dist

# Git
.git
.gitignore

# IDE
.idea
.vscode
*.swp
*.swo

# Environment
# `.env*` rather than `.env` + `.env.*`: also covers `.envrc` (direnv) and `.env-local`,
# matching lt-monorepo's `**/.env*`.
.env*

# Key material — none of these exist today; excluded pre-emptively because this file
# is a template and the cost of finding out the hard way is a key in an image layer.
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
id_rsa*

# NOT excluded, deliberately: `.npmrc`. Its own header declares it the auth/registry
# file, and the deps stage copies it into /app, so excluding it would silently drop
# registry auth. It never reaches the final image (stage 3 copies only dist/ and the
# pruned node_modules) — but a token WOULD land in the `deps` layer, which survives in
# the local builder cache and in any exported BuildKit cache. If this project ever
# needs real registry auth, use `--secret id=npmrc` instead of committing a token.

# Logs
*.log
# Rotated too: `*.log` only matches a name ENDING in `.log`, so `api.log.1` from
# a rotating logger would sail past it.
*.log.*
npm-debug.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# Runtime state — written while the server runs locally, never read by a build.
# `uploads` is the TUS staging directory, i.e. real user documents (it is in
# .gitignore for the same reason, which also means it never shows up in
# `git status` to remind anyone it is sitting in the build context).
uploads
# `lt dev`'s directory: detached server logs + scratch state. The API logs every
# request it serves into it.
.lt-dev

# Testing
tests
coverage
test-results
.nyc_output

# Docker (prevent recursive copy)
Dockerfile*
docker-compose*
.dockerignore

# CI/CD
.gitlab-ci.yml
.gitlab

# Misc
.DS_Store
*.tgz
.husky
.claude
